    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0169" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg87"/>

                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr.
                        Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 267.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 5, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I desire to supply an omission in my
                    despatch No. 257.</p>
                <p>The compliments of condolence and of sympathy addressed to me on the part of the
                    King, as I have since learned from his aide-de-camp, applied also to the crime
                    which nearly cost to the state the life of Secretary Seward.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. S. SANFORD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hunter,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
